@startuml normal-ingestion
title US-08: Normal Ingestion - Poller Publishes Without Blocking

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

collections "OpenSky / AIS\nFeed" as Feed
participant "Ingestion\nPoller" as Poller
queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as KafkaRaw
participant "Position\nConsumer" as PosConsumer
queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as KafkaNorm
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation

Feed -> Poller : position pings (burst)

loop for each ping
  Poller -> KafkaRaw : publish raw event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }
  KafkaRaw --> Poller : ack

  note over Poller
    Poller does not wait for consumers.
    Publishes and moves on immediately.
    No retry or buffer logic needed
    in the poller itself.
  end note
end

note over KafkaRaw
  Events retained for configured
  retention window regardless of
  consumer processing speed.
end note

KafkaRaw -> PosConsumer : consume at own pace\n(consumer group: position-consumer)

note over PosConsumer
  Parses and normalises raw events.
  Routes malformed events to DLQ (see US-09).
  Publishes normalised events downstream.
end note

PosConsumer -> KafkaNorm : publish to position.normalized

KafkaNorm -> Correlation : consume at own pace\n(consumer group: correlation-worker)

note over KafkaRaw, Correlation
  Each stage reads independently from its own offset.
  A slow correlation worker does not block
  the position consumer or the poller.
end note

@enduml
